      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Clearing denominators gives \\( - 4 x - 3 = A \\left(x + 3\\right) + B \\left(x + 1\\right) \\). Setting \\( x = -1 \\) gives \\( A = \\frac{1}{2} \\), and setting \\( x = -3 \\) gives \\( B = - \\frac{9}{2} \\), so the integrand is \\( 1 - \\frac{9}{2 \\left(x + 3\\right)} + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(x + 1\\right)} \\).",
